<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">light</ansi>

How well you can see where you are, and what it means in a fight.

Rooms are dark, dim, or lit, depending on the time of day, the weather,
whether you're indoors, and the light people carry. A torch, a lantern, or
the <ansi fg="command">floatinglight</ansi> spell lights your way. A companion's or ally's light in
your party lights you too.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Fighting in the dark</ansi>

- In <ansi fg="yellow">darkness</ansi>, every blow is 40% less likely to hit.
- In <ansi fg="yellow">dim</ansi> light, 10% less likely.
- A foe carrying a light is easier to see, and counts as no worse than dim.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">light</ansi>
  Show the light here, whether you carry one, and your to-hit penalty.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
